      "notes": {
        "1": "initial kit extraction (yaelfiner shared/, angel, glopus)",
        "10": "Manifest background_color: Android paints it behind the navigation bar",
        "11": "From Angel: drawer footer matches the brand band (--topbar-h) with no drawer bottom padding, optional list snippet, --accent-text; AccountMenu (avatar + name, upward menu with Sign out); App template footer is one row; TopBar height from --topbar-h",
        "12": "Drawer footer order settled: account on the start side; then the one-tap light/dark icon, the version (small, v1.40) and the reload icon on the end. The version moved out of the account menu to sit beside reload, where someone looks when asked which version they're on; the three-way theme picker belongs on a settings page, never the drawer.",
        "13": "No theme_color in the vite.config manifest: an installed Android app paints its navigation bar with it, one colour for both themes; without it the bar follows the phone (verified on Samsung, Emotion Stack, Oct 2026).",
        "14": "Drawer footer order: light/dark, settings gear, reload icon, then the version last. The controls people use come first; the version closes the row right after the reload that fixes a wrong one.",
        "2": "svelte.config.js: no preprocessor",
        "3": "TopBar trailing action (snippet + label + handler)",
        "4": "Drawer groups (titled sections) and count badges",
        "5": "Drawer groups: fix",
        "6": "Drawer: nav list is the scroll region (flex:1, overflow-y auto) so a drawer taller than the screen scrolls while brand and footer stay pinned",
        "7": "Drawer: shadow only while open; a closed drawer's 40px blur shaded the page's start edge",
        "8": "base.css: color-scheme light in :root; apps with dark mode flip it in .dark so native controls (time picker icon) follow",
        "9": "#app pinned with position: fixed; inset: 0 instead of 100dvh (installed Android PWAs report 100dvh 56px taller than the screen); interactive-widget=resizes-content in index.html"
